{"type":"new","contents":"/-\nInfoGeometry/OperatorAlgebra/TomitaCartanDynamics.lean\n\nCartan dynamics into Tomita-center collapse and Krein isotropic defects.\n\nThis module connects the kinematic mechanism isolated in\n`TomitaCartanSplit.lean` to a dynamical Cartan-flow socket:\n\n* noncompact Cartan directions are the antisymmetric Tomita branch;\n* a model may supply a flow saying that such directions hit the\n  algebra/commutant overlap or a Drazin/Tomita defect locus;\n* factor-center exclusion collapses overlap to scalars;\n* a representation bridge maps that collapse to an isotropic vector in the\n  doubled Krein carrier.\n\nThe file deliberately keeps the analytic convergence/limit statement as a\nwitness field.  The algebraic theorem proved here is the composition of those\nwitnesses.\n-/\n\nimport Mathlib\nimport InfoGeometry.OperatorAlgebra.TomitaCartanSplit\n\nnoncomputable section\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.OperatorAlgebra.TomitaCartanSplit\n\nuniverse uOp uGen uH uSplit uCarrier\n\n/-! ## 1. Antisymmetric Cartan routing kills mirror-balanced data -/\n\nnamespace CartanTomitaGenerator\n\nvariable {Op : Type uOp} [Ring Op]\nvariable {T : TomitaCommutantDatum Op}\n\n/--\nA Tomita-doubled generator is mirror-balanced when its algebra and commutant\nrepresentatives coincide in the ambient represented algebra.\n-/\ndef MirrorBalanced\n    (X : CartanTomitaGenerator T) : Prop :=\n  X.mirror = X.localGen\n\n/--\nA noncompact Cartan generator vanishes on the mirror-balanced diagonal.\n\nThis is the operator-level version of `x - x = 0` and is the algebraic source\nof the null/Krein collapse for noncompact Tomita routing.\n-/\ntheorem noncompact_globalGenerator_eq_zero_of_balanced\n    (X : CartanTomitaGenerator T)\n    (hsec : X.sector = CartanSector.noncompact)\n    (hbal : X.MirrorBalanced) :\n    X.globalGenerator = 0 := by\n  dsimp [globalGenerator]\n  rw [hsec]\n  dsimp [mirrorCombination]\n  rw [hbal]\n  simp\n\n/--\nA compact Cartan generator doubles on the mirror-balanced diagonal.\n\nCompact directions are symmetric; they do not produce the antisymmetric\ncancellation responsible for the Krein null readout.\n-/\ntheorem compact_globalGenerator_eq_add_self_of_balanced\n    (X : CartanTomitaGenerator T)\n    (hsec : X.sector = CartanSector.compact)\n    (hbal : X.MirrorBalanced) :\n    X.globalGenerator = X.localGen + X.localGen := by\n  dsimp [globalGenerator]\n  rw [hsec]\n  dsimp [mirrorCombination]\n  rw [hbal]\n\n/--\nEquivalent version using the Tomita mirror field directly.\n-/\ntheorem noncompact_globalGenerator_eq_zero_of_tomita_fixed\n    (X : CartanTomitaGenerator T)\n    (hsec : X.sector = CartanSector.noncompact)\n    (hfixed : T.tomitaMirror X.localGen = X.localGen) :\n    X.globalGenerator = 0 := by\n  apply X.noncompact_globalGenerator_eq_zero_of_balanced hsec\n  dsimp [MirrorBalanced]\n  rw [X.mirror_eq, hfixed]\n\nend CartanTomitaGenerator\n\n/-! ## 2. Cartan flow socket hitting the algebra/commutant overlap -/\n\n/--\nA Cartan dynamics witness saying that noncompact directions reach the\nalgebra/commutant overlap at a supplied hitting time.\n\nThis is intentionally a witness socket.  Analytic statements such as convergence\nof a noncompact one-parameter group to a projective boundary should be proved in\nconcrete models and then supplied through `noncompact_hits_overlap`.\n-/\nstructure CartanDynamicsToOverlap\n    (Gen : Type uGen)\n    (Op : Type uOp) [Ring Op] [SMul ℝ Op]\n    (F : FactorCenterExclusion Op) where\n  /-- Cartan/modular flow generated by a symmetry direction. -/\n  flow : Gen → ℝ → Op → Op\n\n  /-- Compact/noncompact parity of the generator. -/\n  parity : Gen → CartanParity\n\n  /-- Time at which the model declares the overlap/defect boundary is reached. -/\n  hittingTime : Gen → Op → ℝ\n\n  /-- Noncompact Cartan directions reach the algebra/commutant overlap. -/\n  noncompact_hits_overlap :\n    ∀ (X : Gen) (x : Op),\n      parity X = CartanParity.noncompact →\n        flow X (hittingTime X x) x ∈ F.algebra ∧\n        flow X (hittingTime X x) x ∈ F.commutant\n\nnamespace CartanDynamicsToOverlap\n\nvariable\n    {Gen : Type uGen}\n    {Op : Type uOp} [Ring Op] [SMul ℝ Op]\n    {F : FactorCenterExclusion Op}\n\nvariable (D : CartanDynamicsToOverlap Gen Op F)\n\n/-- The boundary/overlap representative reached by the Cartan flow. -/\ndef hit\n    (X : Gen) (x : Op) : Op :=\n  D.flow X (D.hittingTime X x) x\n\n/-- A noncompact Cartan hit belongs to the algebra side. -/\ntheorem noncompact_hit_mem_algebra\n    {X : Gen} {x : Op}\n    (hX : D.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    D.hit X x ∈ F.algebra := by\n  exact (D.noncompact_hits_overlap X x hX).1\n\n/-- A noncompact Cartan hit belongs to the commutant side. -/\ntheorem noncompact_hit_mem_commutant\n    {X : Gen} {x : Op}\n    (hX : D.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    D.hit X x ∈ F.commutant := by\n  exact (D.noncompact_hits_overlap X x hX).2\n\n/--\nA noncompact Cartan hit has zero dynamic part by factor-center exclusion.\n-/\ntheorem noncompact_hit_dynamicPart_zero\n    {X : Gen} {x : Op}\n    (hX : D.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    F.dynamicPart (D.hit X x) = 0 := by\n  exact\n    FactorCenterExclusion.overlap_dynamicPart_zero F\n      (D.noncompact_hit_mem_algebra hX)\n      (D.noncompact_hit_mem_commutant hX)\n\n/--\nA noncompact Cartan hit maps to an isotropic vector under any supplied\ncenter-collapse-to-Krein bridge.\n-/\ntheorem noncompact_hit_isotropic\n    {H : Type uH}\n    [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H]\n    (B : CenterCollapseMapsToIsotropic Op H F)\n    {X : Gen} {x : Op}\n    (hX : D.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    doubledKreinForm (B.carrierReadout (D.hit X x))\n      (B.carrierReadout (D.hit X x)) = 0 := by\n  apply B.dynamic_zero_is_isotropic\n  exact D.noncompact_hit_dynamicPart_zero hX\n\nend CartanDynamicsToOverlap\n\n/-! ## 3. Cartan flow socket hitting a Tomita/Drazin defect locus -/\n\n/--\nA Cartan dynamics witness saying that noncompact directions hit an already\nspecified Tomita defect locus in a split source.\n\nThis is the defect-locus version of `CartanDynamicsToOverlap`.\n-/\nstructure CartanDynamicsToDefect\n    (Gen : Type uGen)\n    (Op : Type uOp) [Ring Op]\n    (Split : Type uSplit)\n    (Carrier : Type uCarrier)\n    [AddCommGroup Carrier] [Module ℝ Carrier]\n    {T : TomitaCommutantDatum Op}\n    (B : TomitaDefectNullBridge Op Split Carrier T) where\n  /-- Cartan/modular flow on the split source. -/\n  flow : Gen → ℝ → Split → Split\n\n  /-- Compact/noncompact parity of the generator. -/\n  parity : Gen → CartanParity\n\n  /-- Time at which the model declares the defect boundary is reached. -/\n  hittingTime : Gen → Split → ℝ\n\n  /-- Noncompact directions reach the supplied defect locus. -/\n  noncompact_hits_defect :\n    ∀ (X : Gen) (a : Split),\n      parity X = CartanParity.noncompact →\n        flow X (hittingTime X a) a ∈ B.defectLocus\n\nnamespace CartanDynamicsToDefect\n\nvariable\n    {Gen : Type uGen}\n    {Op : Type uOp} [Ring Op]\n    {Split : Type uSplit}\n    {Carrier : Type uCarrier}\n    [AddCommGroup Carrier] [Module ℝ Carrier]\n    {T : TomitaCommutantDatum Op}\n    {B : TomitaDefectNullBridge Op Split Carrier T}\n\nvariable (D : CartanDynamicsToDefect Gen Op Split Carrier B)\n\n/-- The defect representative reached by the Cartan flow. -/\ndef hit\n    (X : Gen) (a : Split) : Split :=\n  D.flow X (D.hittingTime X a) a\n\n/-- A noncompact Cartan hit belongs to the supplied defect locus. -/\ntheorem noncompact_hit_mem_defect\n    {X : Gen} {a : Split}\n    (hX : D.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    D.hit X a ∈ B.defectLocus := by\n  exact D.noncompact_hits_defect X a hX\n\n/--\nA noncompact Cartan hit lands in the algebra/commutant overlap through the\nTomita defect bridge.\n-/\ntheorem noncompact_hit_overlap\n    {X : Gen} {a : Split}\n    (hX : D.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    T.InOverlap (B.representedOperator (D.hit X a)) := by\n  exact B.defect_overlap (D.hit X a) (D.noncompact_hit_mem_defect hX)\n\n/--\nA noncompact Cartan hit is scalar through the factor-like Tomita overlap rule.\n-/\ntheorem noncompact_hit_overlap_scalar\n    {X : Gen} {a : Split}\n    (hX : D.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    B.representedOperator (D.hit X a) ∈ T.scalar := by\n  exact B.defect_overlap_scalar (D.noncompact_hit_mem_defect hX)\n\n/--\nA noncompact Cartan hit is null under the supplied carrier quadratic readout.\n-/\ntheorem noncompact_hit_null\n    {X : Gen} {a : Split}\n    (hX : D.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    B.q (B.carrierReadout (D.hit X a)) = 0 := by\n  exact B.defect_is_null (D.noncompact_hit_mem_defect hX)\n\nend CartanDynamicsToDefect\n\n/-! ## 4. Bundled Tomita-Cartan-Krein dynamics theorem -/\n\n/--\nBundled datum connecting Cartan dynamics to the doubled Krein null mechanism.\n\nThis is the canonical witness package:\n\n`noncompact Cartan flow → overlap → scalar collapse → isotropic carrier`.\n-/\nstructure TomitaCartanKreinDynamics\n    (Gen : Type uGen)\n    (Op : Type uOp) [Ring Op] [SMul ℝ Op]\n    (H : Type uH) [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] where\n  /-- Factor-center exclusion data for the represented algebra. -/\n  factor : FactorCenterExclusion Op\n\n  /-- Bridge from scalar/dynamic collapse to Krein isotropy. -/\n  bridge : CenterCollapseMapsToIsotropic Op H factor\n\n  /-- Cartan dynamics reaching the overlap in noncompact directions. -/\n  dynamics : CartanDynamicsToOverlap Gen Op factor\n\nnamespace TomitaCartanKreinDynamics\n\nvariable\n    {Gen : Type uGen}\n    {Op : Type uOp} [Ring Op] [SMul ℝ Op]\n    {H : Type uH} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H]\n\nvariable (W : TomitaCartanKreinDynamics Gen Op H)\n\n/-- The Cartan-flow boundary representative. -/\ndef hit\n    (X : Gen) (x : Op) : Op :=\n  W.dynamics.hit X x\n\n/--\nMain theorem: noncompact Cartan dynamics generates an isotropic doubled-Krein\ncarrier readout.\n\nAll analytic/geometric content is in the supplied witnesses.  The theorem here\nis the formal composition of those witnesses.\n-/\ntheorem noncompact_generates_isotropic\n    {X : Gen} {x : Op}\n    (hX : W.dynamics.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    doubledKreinForm (W.bridge.carrierReadout (W.hit X x))\n      (W.bridge.carrierReadout (W.hit X x)) = 0 := by\n  exact W.dynamics.noncompact_hit_isotropic W.bridge hX\n\n/--\nEquivalent named form: the noncompact hit has zero dynamic part before applying\nits carrier readout.\n-/\ntheorem noncompact_hit_dynamicPart_zero\n    {X : Gen} {x : Op}\n    (hX : W.dynamics.parity X = CartanParity.noncompact) :\n    W.factor.dynamicPart (W.hit X x) = 0 := by\n  exact W.dynamics.noncompact_hit_dynamicPart_zero hX\n\nend TomitaCartanKreinDynamics\n\nend InfoGeometry.OperatorAlgebra.TomitaCartanSplit\n","mtime":1777928003348}